<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan basic metals market - January 6.</title>
<headline>Taiwan basic metals market - January 6.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are prices for key Taiwan base metals as quoted by local traders on Monday:</p>
<p>					January 6	December 3</p>
<p> 2.6 mm copper wire (kg)	   T$73.0	    T$75.0</p>
<p> 8.0 mm copper strip (kg)	  T$71.5	    T$73.5</p>
<p> 2.0 mm electric wire (yard)	T$3.8	     T$3.8</p>
<p> aluminium ingots (kg)	     T$45.5	    T$44.5</p>
<p> Australian zinc (kg)		T$37.0	    T$37.0</p>
<p> tin (kg)			     T$168.0	   T$174.0</p>
<p>Tai-I said it had lowered its 1996 revenue target to T$5.825 billion from T$6.804 billion and its pre-tax profit target to T$170 million from T$283 million.</p>
<p>Officials at Tai-I attributed the drop to the unexpected fall in world copper prices, which in turn depressed domestic prices for copper products. Weak demand from Taiwan's still-sluggish economy was another factor, they said.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-508-0815)</p>
